<title>UK: FORECAST - Has Cadbury's 7UP lost its fizzle?.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Has Cadbury's 7UP lost its fizzle?.</headline>
<byline>Tim Farrand</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soft drinks and confectionery group Cadbury-Schweppes Plc, expected to report a solid eight percent rise in first half profits on Wednesday, faces questions about the performance of its 7UP soft drink in the U.S.</p>
<p>&quot;One of the main questions will be the success or otherwise of the relaunch of the 7UP brand,&quot; said Mark Duffy, food manufacturing analyst at SBC Warburg. Competitor Sprite, owned by Coca-Cola, has seen an agressive marketing push and is ranked the fastest growing brand in the U.S. after Cadbury's Dr Pepper.</p>
</text>
